63baca09dad0d6b0aed631716b3234f9b2a8b92dca5ef16a313a376956df1","event_uuid":"5f4e4bd4-4f12-49da-8b1d-4d6d78ea917c","position":{"commit_sha":"653008a2c5b0202069e25922b966af79f85dc4b2","position":"1788047190108905001-5f4e4bd4-4f12-49da-8b1d-4d6d78ea917c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence for each Acceptance Criteria item:\n- config.py 689 LOC, plan_review/__init__.py 606 LOC (both <=700) via extraction into config_readers.py (137 LOC) / plan_review/floors.py (222 LOC) only -- no other files touched for the split.\n- Neither new module is <100 LOC; both are pure verbatim relocations (no mechanical split, no logic changes).\n- Confirmed via held-out validation (145/148 passed pre-fix) and a live mutation/teeth check: temporarily dropped the config_readers re-export, confirmed test_model_classes.py's monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, ...) tests failed for the right reason (AttributeError), then restored -- all green. Same held-out run proved every plan_review floor-helper monkeypatch seam (rising_floor, completion_floor, sidecar_heldout, blocking_fix_unit_grouping) still intercepts through __init__.py's namespace.\n- test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py's _CONFIG_PY repointed to config_readers.py; test_subcall_class_selection.py's _EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES entry updated to llm/plan_review/floors.py::_score_floor_novelty. Both files pass (18/18).\n- floors.py's _score_floor_novelty / _classify_completion reach _verifier_cfg via a lazy in-function import (from rebar.llm.plan_review import _verifier_cfg); confirmed no circular import at collection time.\n- Full default suite (make test): 18008 passed, 9 failed -- all 9 confirmed pre-existing via git stash against the unmodified tree (unrelated git-subprocess/env failures in test_atomic_completion_close.py / test_rebar_repo_isolation.py / test_tracker_footprint_cli.py). The one failure this change DID cause (test_gate_context_seam.py's no-repoint guard, which didn't yet know about the config_readers.py sibling) was fixed by extending its allowlist with a documented rationale (current_code_root() there is a ContextVar read, never a monkeypatch target) and reverified green.\n- model_classes.py's _read_llm_file_table import verified unchanged and passing (test_model_classes.py, test_model_class_ladder.py green).\n- llm/runner.py not touched (confirmed via git diff --stat on the landed change).\n- make lint, make typecheck both clean; module-size gate (wc -l against .github/module-size-limit.txt=800) and complexity ratchet (scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check: active=39 new=0 increased=0) both pass. Also required a one-line fix to scripts/check_config_ownership.py's composition-root allowlist (config_readers.py wasn't recognized as config.py's sibling) and a docs/env-vars.md regen, both landed in the same change.\n\nLanded as Gerrit change https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2390 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, submitted/merged to main at commit 27cdc312846a).","timestamp":1788046097204487001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788033535584801407,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8ef3bd6a-40b2-4a59-82d4-a6d76f84fe8d","relation":"blocks","target_id":"ec44-b572-1067-4c52"},{"link_uuid":"a64bf2c0-cc31-4437-84d1-d0747a0a4da7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eea5-938e-a5e3-44de"},{"link_uuid":"a3671562-510f-44b8-9c3d-a3f98a2c2da8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4f3c-25c3-471b-4e8c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nMaking OperationSnapshot authoritative for LLM operations (gaudy-working-mantaray) migrates `LLMConfig.from_env` call sites and threads a snapshot-derived projection through the gate/workflow entry points. `src/rebar/llm/config.py` (799 LOC) and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` (796 LOC) are within a few lines of the hard 800-LOC module-size cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so that threading would breach the CI module-size gate on first edit.\n\nCreate headroom FIRST via behavior-preserving extraction along existing call-graph seams. This story adds no snapshot-threading logic; it only relocates existing clusters.\n\n## Approach\n\n- `llm/config.py`: move `_env_truthy`, `_read_llm_file_table`, `_llm_str_source`, `_llm_str`, `_llm_int`, `_llm_float`, `_llm_drain_mode` into a new sibling `llm/config_readers.py`. `config.py` re-imports all of them (`from .config_readers import (...)  # noqa: F401`) at module top, mirroring the existing `gate_context` re-export pattern (config.py L41-47). `LLMConfig.from_env` (the sole caller) is NOT moved, so its bare-name lookups resolve through `config.py`'s own namespace — this is what keeps the ~15 existing `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, \"_read_llm_file_table\", ...)` seams live. `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`'s direct `_read_llm_file_table` import keeps working via the re-export.\n- `llm/plan_review/__init__.py`: move ONLY the five pure leaves — `_apply_floor_to_verdict`, `_score_floor_novelty`, `_apply_completion_floor_to_verdict`, `_classify_completion`, `_group_blocking_fix_units` — into a new sibling `llm/plan_review/floors.py`, re-imported (`from .floors import (...)  # noqa: F401`). `_maybe_apply_rising_floor` and `_maybe_apply_completion_floor` STAY in `__init__.py`: they are the entry points `_run_plan_review` calls, and their internal bare-name calls into the five moved leaves must keep resolving through `__init__.py`'s namespace so `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_score_floor_novelty\"/\"_classify_completion\", ...)` (test_plan_review_rising_floor.py, test_completion_floor.py) keeps intercepting. `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"_maybe_apply_rising_floor\"/\"_maybe_apply_completion_floor\"/\"_group_blocking_fix_units\", ...)` (test_plan_review_sidecar_heldout.py) is unaffected either way since its caller `_run_plan_review` also stays put.\n- **`_verifier_cfg`** stays in `__init__.py` (used elsewhere there too). The two moved leaves that call it (`_score_floor_novelty`, `_classify_completion`) reach it via a **lazy in-function import** (`from rebar.llm.plan_review import _verifier_cfg`), not a module-top-level import — `__init__.py` already does `from .floors import (...)` at its own top, so a reverse top-level import in `floors.py` would cycle. By call time the package is fully initialized, so the lazy import is safe; this mirrors the lazy-import style these two functions already use for `rebar.llm.runner`/`review_kernel.verify`/`passes`.\n\n`LLMConfig`, `review_plan`, and public plan_review imports keep working unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/` — new sibling modules (`config_readers.py`, `plan_review/floors.py`); import updates only. Does NOT touch `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` (owned by hurt-antigorite-genet).\n- `tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/` — import-path updates only, EXCEPT two consumers that pin a physical path/text and must be repointed:\n  - `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py` AST-parses `config.py`'s source TEXT by path (`_CONFIG_PY`) to enumerate `_llm_*` helpers; repoint `_CONFIG_PY` to `config_readers.py` (or also parse it) so the moved names keep being found.\n  - `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`'s `_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES` hard-codes `'llm/plan_review/__init__.py::_score_floor_novelty'`; update to `'llm/plan_review/floors.py::_score_floor_novelty'`.\n\n## Testing\n\nExisting llm/plan-review suites (`tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/`) pass unchanged — every `monkeypatch.setattr(rebar.llm.config, \"_read_llm_file_table\", ...)` site and every `monkeypatch.setattr(plan_review, \"<floor-helper>\", ...)` site (rising-floor, completion-floor, completion-floor-e2e, blocking-fix-unit-grouping, sidecar-heldout tests) keeps intercepting the same call. The two path-pinning consumers above are updated and continue to pass. Module-size gate, complexity ratchet, lint, typecheck pass. No new CI-provider/network/Docker dependency.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `config.py` and `plan_review/__init__.py` are each <= 700 LOC via extraction into `config_readers.py` / `plan_review/floors.py` only.\n- [x] No new module < 100 LOC; no mechanical split.\n- [x] Every existing monkeypatch seam on a moved helper via its ORIGINAL module keeps intercepting the same call site.\n- [x] `test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py`'s `_CONFIG_PY` control and `test_subcall_class_selection.py`'s `_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES` entry are updated to the new locations and pass.\n- [x] `floors.py` reaches `_verifier_cfg` via a lazy in-function import; no top-level circular import with `__init__.py`.\n- [x] Behavior unchanged across `tests/unit/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/external/`.\n- [x] `model_classes.py`'s `_read_llm_file_table` import keeps working unchanged.\n- [x] `llm/runner.py` untouched.\n- [x] Module-size gate, complexity ratchet, lint, typecheck all pass.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"Extract primitive env/file reader helpers into a sibling so from_env threading has headroom."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"Extract the score-floor / completion-floor cluster into a sibling to create headroom."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py","reason":"New sibling module holding the extracted env/file reader helpers."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/floors.py","reason":"New sibling module holding the extracted score-floor / completion-floor helpers."},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"Extend the composition-root allowlist to recognize config_readers.py as config.py's sibling (same pattern as _config_sources.py/_config_resolvers.py)."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","ec44-b572-1067-4c52"],["parent","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"],["relates_to","4f3c-25c3-471b-4e8c"],["relates_to","eea5-938e-a5e3-44de"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","parent_status_uuid":"b16d5a42-6141-4476-a486-1c8a2f94fb74","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["llm","refactor","module-size"],"ticket_id":"02b7-82ef-ca69-4aa8","ticket_type":"story","title":"Create llm config-threading module-size headroom before the authoritative-snapshot cutover","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2ad967ea-d323-4235-a06b-4d921ebebdef","26d42b75-54ff-4bb7-b6e6-a6e4132e1ff7","ee8f5587-916f-4b01-ab4a-19432c1c55b9","85eecec3-8e9b-44fd-8f98-40aeb7fc9ea0","df3a54b8-e228-4576-ab10-26e7e655d90c","a64bf2c0-cc31-4437-84d1-d0747a0a4da7","a3671562-510f-44b8-9c3d-a3f98a2c2da8","4c86f82b-7954-45a4-b152-5bf321b0a47d","d09ec4e3-b2b2-4024-8452-19a348c34665","4b98ad15-991f-4ef8-989d-b58d497aa1f1","71bd0824-b41c-4f89-ada0-4190f07bbf29","b16d5a42-6141-4476-a486-1c8a2f94fb74","5f4e4bd4-4f12-49da-8b1d-4d6d78ea917c"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788049898561165423,"uuid":"095e189d-ea8f-4d84-83b4-994e9ceab0dc"}